# The MXFP4 x Q8_2_X4 single-core rate, never measured: the v4host round's
# prediction (docs/plan-ledger.md:1285, "미측정") read against its measured
# anchor. Anchor (measured): Q3_K x Q8_K single-core qdot-rate 10.8 GB/s
# (rig-log log/2026-09-20.md:8, MUL-26, 360,448 rows x 880 B). Low edge
# [derived]: the instruction-ratio scaling 10.8 x (136/110) x (130/136) ~ 12.8
# GB/s — MXFP4 carries 136 B and ~136 instructions per 256 values where Q3_K
# carries 110 B and ~130. High edge [derived]: the MXFP4 inner loop's
# vector-pipe census (~30 cycles per 256 values, loads not binding) carrying
# Q3_K's measured inefficiency (46 cycles measured vs ~30-33 bound, x1.4) ->
# ~42 cycles -> ~9.3 ns per 136 B ~ 14.6 GB/s. Break-even [derived, r4design
# §7 "qdot 항"]: the decode host leg stays DRAM-bound while the per-core rate
# clears ~7.8 GB/s — t(m) = max(W, a + c·m) at m = 1 has W 92-99 µs (13.37 MB
# per expert at 135-145 GB/s) against a + c = 40.4 + 30.2 µs, so the leg tips
# only at c' <= 51.8 µs per expert-column.
# Measured 2026-10-10 (the m2-mxfp4-tile sitting, qdot-rate, one pinned core, 3
# rounds; witness loadavg ~13, not a quiet box): the band ~~12.8-14.6~~ GB/s
# below is struck; 10.1-10.2 GB/s at k = 2048 and 10.4-10.8 at k = 4096, under
# the band and above the 7.8 break-even (decide-in's DRAM-bound leg holds; the
# "between 7.8 and 12.8" branch: profile qdot-rate first); ik's mxfp4_x4_rate
# 11.1-11.4 GB/s at k = 2048 in the same lease.
kind: calibration
question: does the MXFP4 x Q8_2_X4 dot's single-core rate keep MiMo-V2.6-Flash's
  decode host leg bound by host DRAM — per-core rate at or above the ~7.8 GB/s
  break-even, inside the predicted band?
term: qdot-rate single-thread GB/s of MXFP4 rows at k = 4096 (MiMo
  ffn_gate/up_exps, 2176 B/row) and k = 2048 (MiMo ffn_down_exps, 1088 B/row),
  360,448 rows x 6 passes per arm, one pinned core (BLOOMERY_RATE_CORE), the
  runner's rounds alternating with ik's mxfp4_x4_rate in one lease
unit: GB/s
predict: 12.8..14.6
condition: the lead runs, after just build-ref (so mxfp4_x4_rate exists),
  BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/m2-mxfp4-rate.card'
  just measure-qdot-rate 3 on this tree — the recipe builds qdot-rate itself,
  the runner pins one core and reverses arm order every round, and the witness
  shows no other compute on the box
reason: sets qdot's MXFP4 per-column cost c in docs/plan.md:77's host-union row
  (t(m) = max(W, a + c·m)) and closes plan-ledger.md:1285's "미측정" (MXFP4
  12.8-14.6); why now: the rate decides whether MiMo's card-expert round (R5)
  or an MXFP4 decode kernel round comes first, and it is the prompt-path round
  (R8)'s first lever
decide-in: the decode leg is DRAM-bound; record the rate in plan-ledger.md's
  v4host line and in plan.md's host-union row; R5 (card experts) next; an
  MXFP4 tile only in the R8 prompt-path round
decide-below: under 7.8 GB/s the decode leg is ALU-bound and an MXFP4 decode
  kernel round comes before R5; between 7.8 and 12.8 a term the derivation
  missed: profile qdot-rate (perf -e cpu-clock) before deciding
decide-above: rewrite the MXFP4 c in plan.md's host-union row and re-derive
  MiMo's prompt-path (R8) prediction
